<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Northern War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1655">1655</a>–<a href="/years/1660">1660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as First Northern War, Northern War of 1655–1660</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Northern War (1655–1660) was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-x-gustav">Charles X Gustav</a> and its adversaries, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">The Great Elector</a> changed sides from Sweden to Poland and won full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-prussia">Duchy of Prussia</a> by the treaties of Labiau and Wehlau in 1656–1657, confirmed at the Peace of Oliva in 1660.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-northern-war.jpg" alt="Second Northern War" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imonoz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_Northern_War.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
